  "steps": [
    "The event animation starter previews every exact script byte. Its event and clip parameters, selected path and existing character document type persist in Chinese, English and Japanese at 390px; the final source line is reachable by scrolling. Return/Create/Cancel remain visible. Cancel changes no editor state or author files.",
    "Create script opens the normal TXT source draft and focuses its editor without any file or registration write. Ordinary Save stores the reviewed GDScript bytes under the existing character type, adds only source plus registration, and immediately makes that source visible to the existing behavior source directory.",
    "The existing first-behavior UI reviews and cancels without writes, then saves one binding to the new script in one explicit transaction. It creates only the behavior source and registration plus the scene relationship. Open enters the ordinary behavior source editor.",
    "Event name remains an ordinary string. The saved animation directory offers clips by name, interval and full UUID; tentative selection does not fill clip_id, and explicit insertion does. Three languages at390px retain field nodes, selection, values and complete review. Cancel leaves the created behavior source unchanged.",
    "Applying the reviewed parameters changes only the normal source draft. Ordinary Save persists exact reviewed behavior bytes, reopening retains event_name and clip_id, and the new starter script plus every other author file remain unchanged. Engine execution is tested separately."
  ],
